{"code_commit": "29ed22088af2fc0041a5a286f792e29c5b87de45", "correction": "Post-results disclosure correction, no analysis change. Every phase-1 writer arm (T+, S+, no-evidence search control, generic note) received TASK_TEXT (slh/xp/partner/learners.py) stating the target rules: for sequence that the address change must come first, and for address/variant that a change is written when the user has approved it. The agent never received TASK_TEXT directly. The implementation was pinned (amendment 2, source a68f899), but the registration prose and docs/xp/conventions.md wrongly said the conventions were not given to any arm in words. Also: the same-length generic note falls back to B1 when a library is under 250 tokens, and the person-written procedures state the conventions (an upper reference). The registered contrasts and verdicts are unchanged; the interpretation 'learning unwritten conventions' is withdrawn in favour of 'episode evidence improves lessons beyond search when writers already receive rule-bearing task descriptions'.", "dated_utc": "2026-10-17", "event": "phase1_disclosure_correction", "files_sha256": {"docs/xp/conventions.md": "c43fd4dfc99deed108ca71d1d380c0e703ecfc7f9201f420f413436b5b555e91", "slh/xp/partner/learners.py": "f5a23858b72f2c2d279dff77cd3b2167fbfc34fa598ad65106958c8d399fc348"}, "owner_approval": "2026-10-17 (chat)", "phase1_tag": "xp-p1-v1", "plan_id": "xp-p1-2026-10-10", "prev_sha256": "895a442e3a70659c6e92b471b41584d6858027ba70bcf2d73eeba596aa983be7"}
{"code_commit": "529b7ad700cd9395f64c55e25bd9b26c8bcbb052", "dated_utc": "2026-10-17", "event": "phase2_retired", "files_sha256": {"docs/xp/calibration-2026-10-17.md": "6324816779ec17a05984b25253d22fb34939bd8887b705e9ed3e852bd4d4bb78", "docs/xp/official-tau2-2026-10-17/analysis.md": "11df3ea2493226fef75ca77e142ee1360cf5b478440a023e89a9ee52065072fc", "docs/xp/official-tau2-2026-10-17/score.json": "b0f1c0c7524b24efc00e8f33d43e312e7bf859df731037c4d203edebce4c0f2c", "docs/xp/registration-phase2-draft.md": "3fc9d528e7397e27df4ee60c009402153fe4f896120ecefa8317c5153d46842f"}, "owner_approval": "2026-10-17 (chat)", "plan_id": "xp-p2-v1", "prev_sha256": "263b3996222fa99ed7a9ad44e869e85764d219a05140757fe037dc93672337f7", "status": "Phase-2 confirmatory run retired before registration and before any test conversation. It was never registered and package-p2 was never shipped or run. Reason: three calibration rounds and the official tau2 retail run showed the frozen phase-1 lessons do not change conversation-level success (official pass^1 82.9 vs 81.6), the only arm-discriminating failure was write-before-authentication (now removed by a deterministic guard), and hard-scenario pools were depleted. Reported as a transfer result, not a completed confirmation. The unshipped generated test scenarios may be reused as fresh private evaluation data for later, separately registered work."}
